            <div style={{position:'relative',display:'flex',minWidth:0}}><div className="ctside" ref={railRef} onScroll={railCheck} style={sideColStyle}>{landBars&&pBar(topColor,true)}{_blurbs}{_controls}{landBars&&pBar(bottomColor,false)}</div>{railMore&&(/* #549 item (25) A3-R2, jobs/landscape-puzzle-prev-next-unnamed-and-under-the-tab-bar-2026-11-03: the chip hangs BELOW the rail's clip, in the strip between the rail and the tab bar (about 22px at 730x375, 844x390, 667x375 and 956x440), not inside it. Sticky inside the scroller it sat ON the last visible row - at 844x390 it covered the Show button, whose centre hit-tested to the chip (antagonist A, round 2). Outside the scroller it covers no rail control at rest and adds no height to the rail, so it still cannot change the answer it reports. The wrapper is display:flex with minWidth:0 so the rail shrinks exactly as it did as a direct flex item. */<button data-ct="rail-more" onClick={()=>{const e=railRef.current;if(e)e.scrollBy({top:Math.round(e.clientHeight*0.8),behavior:'smooth'});}} aria-label="More below - scroll" style={{position:'absolute',top:'100%',marginTop:1,left:'50%',transform:'translateX(-50%)',zIndex:5,padding:'2px 12px',lineHeight:1.2,borderRadius:14,border:'1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.25)',background:'rgba(16,18,24,.94)',color:'#cfe0ff',fontSize:12,fontWeight:800,cursor:'pointer',boxShadow:'0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.45)',whiteSpace:'nowrap'}}>▾ More below</button>)}</div>
